Pymtheg patch 0014 (C-21, not upstream): a turbofish in a struct pattern.

Accepts valid Rust: `let ErrorPayload::<serde_json::Value> { message, .. } = p;`
A struct pattern's path may carry generic arguments, as a tuple-struct
pattern's already may (upstream PR #254). Read as
`struct_pattern(type: generic_type(..))`, like the tuple-struct case.
Reference: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/patterns.html#struct-patterns
Upstream pull request: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/pull/301
(open; this is its struct-pattern grammar line only; its attribute change
overlaps PR #319, already taken as patch 0001). Tuple-struct patterns got
the turbofish in https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/pull/254.

diff --git a/grammar.js b/grammar.js
index f812aa8..0cb98dc 100644
--- a/grammar.js
+++ b/grammar.js
@@ -1487,6 +1487,9 @@ module.exports = grammar({
       field('type', choice(
         $._type_identifier,
         $.scoped_type_identifier,
+        // Pymtheg patch 0014 (from upstream PR #301): a turbofish, as
+        // tuple_struct_pattern already allows (`S::<T> { .. }`).
+        alias($.generic_type_with_turbofish, $.generic_type),
       )),
       '{',
       sepBy(',', choice($.field_pattern, $.remaining_field_pattern)),
